WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.093
Complex models are built from small operations. A computational graph names these intermediate values and records

00:00:07.093 --> 00:00:13.987
which outputs depend on which inputs. You can then differentiate each simple edge instead of expanding

00:00:13.987 --> 00:00:15.710
the entire final expression.

00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:21.905
Use a distinct name for each intermediate. Values recorded in the forward pass will be needed

00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:23.323
in the backward calculation.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:29.523
The target five is fixed. The one-half factor makes the derivative of the square especially simple.

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:35.422
If the prediction exceeds its target, what sign should the weight gradient have here? Pause here

00:00:35.422 --> 00:00:37.443
and make a prediction before continuing.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:45.142
Each derivative describes one edge. One is loss sensitivity to the prediction; the other is prediction

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:51.307
sensitivity to the weight. For our starting inputs, Prediction: 7. Loss: 2. Weight gradient: 4.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:57.990
The chain rule combines these sensitivities. In a branching graph, contributions from every path into a

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.913
shared value must be summed.

00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:07.407
Draw the forward computation before differentiating. The graph and its shapes determine the chain-rule factors and

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:07.843
transposes.

